    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "UNITED\nUNITED\nN8005U\nUNITED\nCa NEeD C'8 JETARAMA\npresenting the BEST OF THE JETS the DC-8 JET MAINLINER by DOUGLAS",
      "yes, the best of the jets is here... UNITED AIR LINES\nDC 8 JET MAINLINER\nTHE FIRST JETLINER DESIGNED SPECIFICALLY FOR PASSENGER SERVICE\nThe combined experience of Douglas Aircraft Company.\nPratt and Whitney and United Air Lines has been planned\ninto the DC-8 Jet Mainliner, truly the newest, finest—\nthe best of the jets. The DC-8, designed exclusively for\npassenger service is a worthy successor to the long\nline of proven \"D\" planes which carry four\nout of five of the world's air travelers.\n- FIRST CLASS\nENTRANCE\n- FIRST CLASS\nLOUNGE\n• BUFFET\nFORWARD REST\nROOMS\n-FIRST CLASS\nCABIN\nTHE RED CARPET ROOM\nMost luxurious lounge of any jetliner\nis located far ahead of the swept-\nback wing and extends across the\nfull width of the airplane.\nThis \"room with a view\" styled\nby Raymond Loewy, invites\nfun and relaxation.\nUNITED\n- COACH CABIN\nONE OF THE NATION'S\nFINEST DINING PLACES\nDinner time on first-class\nRed Carpet flights presents\na culinary masterpiece.\nMenus rivaling those of\nthe nation's finest dining\nplaces are set off by rich\ndamask cloths, sparkling\nsilver and fine china.\n- COACH LOUNGE\n- BUFFET\nCOACH ENTRANCE\n•AFT REST ROOMS\nQUALITY COACH SERVICE\nThe coach cabin of United's\nDC-8 Jet Mainliner con-\ntinues the rich decor of\ncustom design.\nHandsomely tailored seats\noffer generous leg room and\nbuilt-in seat conveniences,\nincluding individual fold-\ndown tables for your\nCustom Coach meal service.\nUNITED\nAIR LINES\nDC-8\nJET MAINLINER BY DOUGLAS",
      "BUT IT TAKES MORE THAN A JET AIRLINER TO MAKE A JET AIR LINE\nUNITED\nDC-8 SPECIFICATIONS\nWing Span 142 feet 5 inches\nOverall length\n150 feet 6 inches\nOverall height\n42 feet 4 inches\nWing sweepback\n30 Degrees\nTotal Cargo Volume,\n2 lower compartments\n1162 cubic feet\nPower Plants\n(Pratt \u0026 Whitney J 57)\n4 Turbojet Engines\n(Pratt \u0026 Whitney J 75)\nGross Weight, pounds\n265,000 to 300,000\nLanding Weight, pounds\n190,000\nFuel Capacity, Pounds\n117,900\nFuel Capacity, Gallons\n17,600\nCruise True Air Speed,\nmiles per hour\n516 to 591\nNEW CONCEPT FOR CARGO\nThe DC-8 carries up to 11 pre-\nloaded containers with a total\ncargo capacity of 19,465 pounds.\nEach container can be loaded and\nhandled individually providing the\nfastest, most modern baggage sys-\ntem available.\nPLANNING FOR THE JET AGE\nUnited Air Lines began prepara-\ntion for the jet age long before re-\nceiving the first DC-8 Jet Main-\nliner. Electronic devices like this\nLink flight simulator have given\nhours of valuable\nexperience to\nUnited personnel in addition to\ntheir normal equipment indoctri-\nnation.\n2001.039.213a",
      "INSTAMATIC\nUNITED'S INSTANT RESERVATIONS SYSTEM",
      "UNITED\nAIR LINES\n®\n2001.039. 2136",
      "UNITED\nNEW HIGH-SPEED RESERVATIONS SERVICE\nFOR JET AGE TRAVELERS\nINSTAMATIC was developed especially for United\nAir Lines by The Teleregister Corporation. It will\nbe the world's largest integrated data processing\nsystem\ndeveloped for private industry.\nThe Central\nProcessor\nsite will be located at\nUnited's Operating\nBase in Denver and will con-\nsist of three transistorized Telefile® Processors.\nINSTAMATIC'S 12,000 miles of leased lines will\nFrom\nthis\nelectronic console United agents will be able to confirm your\nreservations in a few seconds from any major city on the Main Line Airway.\nspeed inquiries from 1,000 agent sets at 150 loca-\ntions in 68 cities nationwide into the Central\nProcessor at the amazing speed of 15 inquiries\nper second, or the equivalent of 54,000 messages\nper hour. The average response time to an inquiry\nwill be 1½ seconds.\nINSTAMATIC will operate 24 hours a day and\nwill be another progressive step to bring you\n\"Extra Care\" on the ground and aloft.\nUNITED\nAIR LINES"
    ],
